WEBVTT

00:00:02.065 --> 00:00:10.800
Corporate Advisory
Run a corporate finance mandate behind the advisory information barrier — from pitch to investor commitments.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.320
Sign in as Camille Rivalland — Corporate Advisor
Corporate advisor — Genesis Corporate Advisors

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.640
Corporate Advisory ▸ Advisory Mandates: every deal is known by its code name
Only the advisory team and Compliance can open this module's records

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:34.720
Code name, client, target and service line
Fees: a retainer plus a success fee on the amount raised

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:42.000
Move the mandate along its pipeline
Origination ▸ Pitch ▸ Conflict check

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.760
Pitch won — before any engagement, Compliance must check for conflicts
Moving to Conflict check opens a conflict check for Compliance automatically

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.960
Try to go straight to Engagement letter…
The CRM checks the conflict-check result first

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.400
Blocked: Compliance must clear the conflict check first
No engagement letter can be issued on an unchecked deal

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.640
The conflict check CC-2026-000014 is waiting for Compliance
Compliance is notified and has two business days to decide

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.520
Compliance reviews the conflict check
Compliance sits inside the advisory barrier — it sees every deal

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.280
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance officer — decides conflict checks

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.440
The CRM has already searched the group for conflicts
The client's and target's Genesis relationships, loans outstanding and other advisory mandates

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:20.160
…and the restricted and watch lists
A match here would need controls — or a decline

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:27.400
Take it into review, then record the decision
Requested ▸ Compliance review

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:35.600
Record the decision and the rationale
Cleared · Cleared with controls · Declined

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.800
Decided: the check moves to Decided with the date
The decision is written back to the mandate and kept as the audit record

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.640
What does the trading desk see?
Traders are on the public side of the wall

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:49.240
Sign in as Arvind Ramsurrun — Trader
Trader — public side of the wall

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:54.960
No mandates at all — not even that Project Ravenala exists
Deal records, documents and alerts stay inside the barrier

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.000
Someone who needs inside information asks for a wall-crossing
Tools ▸ Access & Barriers ▸ Wall-crossings

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.080
Approval is time-limited and never by the requester
Once approved, the person is added to the insider list until the crossing ends

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.080
Compliance decides the request
Compliance runs the control room — it approves crossings without seeing behind the wall

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:15.960
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance officer — decides wall-crossings

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.560
Approve for 30 days — the trader joins the advisory insider list until then
Nobody can approve their own request, or a crossing for themselves

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.080
The crossing is recorded on the tamper-evident audit trail
It ends automatically on its expiry date

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.040
Back to the advisor: the conflict check is cleared
Conflict check ▸ Engagement letter

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:38.080
Sign in as Camille Rivalland — Corporate Advisor
Corporate advisor

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:47.680
The engagement letter is generated for you — under the code name
Mandate ▸ Docs, ready for e-signature

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:54.200
Execution needs the signed letter
Try to move on before it is signed…

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.600
Blocked: the engagement letter must be signed first

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:10.360
The client has signed: tick "Engagement letter signed"

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:20.760
Add the analyst to the deal team
Corporate Advisory ▸ Deal Team Member ▸ New

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.720
Ryan Pillay is on the insider list automatically
With the date and the reason — the list the regulator asks for

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:36.120
Approach an investor: Sunrise Pension Fund
Targeted ▸ NDA ▸ IM shared ▸ Indication ▸ Committed ▸ Allocated

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:40.800
The NDA has been sent to the investor
Targeted ▸ NDA

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.320
Share the information memorandum already?
The CRM checks the NDA first

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:48.800
Blocked: the IM can only be shared once the NDA is signed
Inside information never leaves without a signed NDA

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.120
The investor signs the NDA: record it with the date the IM is shared

00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:04.040
Share the IM by secure link
Investor ▸ Docs: upload the IM, then Share link

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:14.160
A link that expires in 14 days, view-only
Every view is counted — you see who has opened the IM

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.800
NDA signed and IM shared: the move is accepted now

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:36.320
The investor indicates MUR 150 million, then commits MUR 120 million
Each stage asks for its figure — indication, commitment, allocation

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.720
Commitments roll up to the mandate and the dashboard

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.840
The information memorandum is a deliverable with a milestone fee
Drafting ▸ In review ▸ Approved ▸ Delivered to client

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:53.760
Name the reviewer: approval needs one
A second pair of eyes on everything that goes to the client

00:04:53.760 --> 00:05:03.040
Drafted, reviewed and approved
Drafting ▸ In review ▸ Approved

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:08.160
Delivered to the client — the milestone fee is invoiced automatically

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.360
Fee invoice raised: MUR 750,000 milestone, sent to accounting
Retainer and success-fee invoices are kept here too

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:22.640
Log the hours spent on the mandate
For profitability: hours × internal rate = cost

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:29.840
The mandate adds it all up
Deal team, insiders, investors, commitments, fees invoiced and hours logged

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:42.880
The Corporate Advisory dashboard
Live mandates, weighted fee pipeline, commitments and fees invoiced

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.840
Mandates by stage and service line, bookbuilding and hours by mandate
Barrier-aware: the public side sees none of it

00:05:47.903 --> 00:05:55.560
Corporate Advisory
Deals stay discreet and controlled — the CRM enforces the wall and the gates.
